  "verbalization": "Tretamine is implicated in the biological pathway leading to FaDu through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Tretamine acts as a target for Cytochrome c oxidase subunit 6A2, mitochondrial, which in turn is targeted by a complex natural compound, (1R,2S,4R,8R,10S,11R,13S)-11-hydroxy-2,11-dimethyl-7-methylidene-5,14-dioxatetracyclo[8.4.0.01,13.04,8]tetradecan-6-one. This compound is also a target of Ganoderic Acid K, which ultimately leads to the interaction with FaDu. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism where Tretamine indirectly influences FaDu through a chain of targets, suggesting a complex, multi-step relationship that may involve metabolic or signaling pathways. The evidence supports a dependency on these molecular intermediates, underscoring the role of these compounds in the biological process linking Tretamine to FaDu.",
